            "review_title": "Review at Gio Bien Restaurant",
            "review_text": "JimmyDevasia\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam223 contributions\n1\nFresh Seafood Nha Trang style\nJan 2016 • Friends\nThis place isn't much known amongst the foreign tourists, but seems to be a hit with the Vietnamese (local and tourists). It is a classic Vietnamese-style seafood joint, with small tables and plastic chairs overflowing onto the pavement. It isn't exactly in the centre of 'foreigner town', but is quite easily accessible, one can't miss it near the roundabout where Tran Phu continues to become Pham Van Dong.\nAs is standard, the sea food is alive and one can choose which one to get cooked according to one's preference. We went for squid, snail and oysters, which cost us an inexpensive 100k vnd per head.\nThe food itself was fresh and prepared well enough, for me to visit next time!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 25, 2016",
